-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",299,{
[9537]="7000EF7C\n1\tCollect Ore (total: 8)\tSearch for ore-bearing rocks in the area surrounding Pynti-leiri.\n2\tBring the Ore to Turkka\tBring the ore you have collected to Turkka in Pynti-leiri.\n",
[9538]="7007163C\n1\tDefeat Utûgi in Emax Dûl (total: 10)\030Defeat Achárbam, the Blood-hand\tThe Utûgi have arrived to regain control of Emax Dûl for their Thardúth masters. You should defeat the Utûgi and their captain, Achárbam, the Blood-hand, in Emax Dûl.\n2\tTalk to Razâl\tThe Utûgi's efforts in Emax Dûl have been disrupted. You should return to Razâl at Nashûbu.\n",
[9539]="70047A81\n1\tDefeat Orcs within Skoironk (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found within the caverns of Skoironk. You should defeat Orcs within Skoironk.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Orcs within Skoironk.\n",
[9540]="7005F6BB\n1\tDefeat glow-worms in Ormgren\tGlow-worms can be found in Ormgren in Gloomingtarn. While exploring Ormgren, you have encountered a massive number of glow-worms dwelling among the ancient ore-lodes of Mount Gundabad. You should defeat glow-worms in Ormgren.\n2\tDefeat glow-worms in Ormgren (total: 24)\tGlow-worms can be found in Ormgren in Gloomingtarn. While exploring Ormgren, you have encountered a massive number of glow-worms dwelling among the ancient ore-lodes of Mount Gundabad. You should defeat glow-worms in Ormgren.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many glow-worms in Ormgren.\n",
[9541]="7003E409\n1\tFertilize Orofarnë's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Acquire handfuls of moss from bog-lurkers (total: 6)\tMoss was once used to protect growing trees from insects. Moss can be found along the river.\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n3\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what mulch is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n4\tFertilize Orofarnë's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Acquire Norbog-mulch (total: 6)\tQuickbeam wishes to next honour his friend by treating his seed with mulch made from Nerbyg. Nerbyg can be found in the northern area of Fangorn.\n5\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n6\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what mulch is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n7\tFertilize Orofarnë's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Acquire sickle-fly mulch (total: 6)\tQuickbeam wishes to next honour his friend by treating his seed with mulch made from sickle-flies. Sickle-flies can be found in the southern area of Fangorn.\n8\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n9\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what mulch is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n10\tFertilize Orofarnë's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Acquire handfuls of moss (quantity: see journal)\030Acquire Norbog-mulch (quantity: see journal)\030Acquire sickle-fly mulch (quantity: see journal)\tQuickbeam wishes to finally honour his friend by treating his seed with moss and both mulches. Moss can be found along the river. Nerbyg can be found in northern Fangorn. Sickle-flies can be found in the southern area of Fangorn.\n11\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam is at Derndingle.\n",
[9542]="7000A147\n1\tTalk to Basil Gummidge\tBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod, located in Tyrn Fornech along the road that runs north of the cross-roads in Parth Aduial, north-east of Tinnudir. Kelsey West has asked you to travel to Ost Forod to speak with Basil Gummidge and offer your help to the people there.\n",
[9543]="70000041\n1\tTalk to Candac Brightwood\tThe Forsaken Inn can be found along the road to the west. Go to the Forsaken Inn and talk to Candac Brightwood.\n",
[9544]="70025B7B\n1\tComplete Writs of Honour\030Complete Unfulfilled Duty\030Complete Payment of an Ancient Debt\tTorogethir is at his camp in Parth Aduial. Torogethir has several tasks he wishes you to complete for him.\n2\tTalk to Torogethir in Parth Aduial\tTorogethir is at his camp in Parth Aduial. Torogethir will want to speak to you about what happened at Ost Heryn.\n",
[9545]="7002F306\n1\tDefeat Orcs and Uruks in Ost Magol (total: 10)\tOrcs and uruks can be found at Ost Magol. Aldbéort asked you to venture into Ost Magol and defeat the Orcs and Uruks within.\n2\tTalk to Aldbéort\tAldbéort is at Cliving. Aldbéort will be pleased to hear the Orcs and Uruks in Ost Magol have been defeated.\n",
[9546]="700310C1\n1\tDestroy a totem in Ost Magol\tTotems can be found in the ruins of Ost Magol. Aldbéort asked you to venture into Ost Magol and destroy the Orc-totems within.\n2\tTalk to Aldbéort\tAldbéort is in Cliving. Aldbéort will be pleased to hear the Orc totems in Ost Magol have been destroyed.\n",
[9547]="7003E515\n1\tSearch Ost Thondol for the source of the evil Pothlorn sensed\tThe ruins of Ost Thondol can be found atop the hill, north-west of Pothlorn. Pothlorn asked you to search the ruins of Ost Thondol for the evil he sensed during his battle with the Stone-trolls.\n2\tDefeat the worm-wight\tThe worm-wight is in the ruins of Ost Thondol, north-west of Pothlorn's hiding place. You should attempt to destroy the worm-wight, which appears to be leading the trolls of Ost Thondol.\n3\tTalk to Pothlorn\tPothlorn is hiding among the rocks at the base of the hill, south-east of Ost Thondol. You should return to Pothlorn and let him know what you discovered within Ost Thondol.\n4\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan is at Thorenhad, north-west of Pothlorn's hiding place. Pothlorn told you to return to Elladan and tell him what you discovered.\n",
[9548]="7000C384\n1\tTalk to Glorwen in the Goblin-town prison\030Talk to the goblin Oghûk in the Goblin-town prison\tThe Elf-maiden and the goblin-prisoner are both in the dungeons of Goblin-town. Aeglas seems unconcerned that he is captured by the goblins of Goblin-town. His concerns are more for the other prisoners within the depths, and he has asked you to discover what the others know of the unrest moving through the goblins of Goblin-town.\n2\tTalk to Aeglas in his cell in the Goblin-town prison\tReturn to Aeglas within his cell in the Goblin-town prison. Oghûk seemed an untrusting sort and offered no information unless you helped him. Glorwen seemed in good spirits, once she knew that Aeglas lived, and provided some important information. You should return at once to Aeglas.\n",
[9549]="7003E787\n1\tFind the dwarf keep of Othrikar\tOthrikar can be found to the north-east of Orthonn's camp, in the northern hills of the Kingsfell. You should seek the dwarf fortress of Othrikar.\n",
[9550]="70071629\n1\tTalk to Kotráka Saiya to be escorted to the palace\tTo safely enter Emax Dûl, you must be escorted across the bridge by Kotráka Saiya. You should talk to Kotráka Saiya at the bridge-fort when you are ready to go.\n2\tTalk to Kotráka Saiya\tYou have arrived inside the palace. You should talk to Kotráka Saiya.\n3\tSecure Lokóya and Adúri\030Secure Otibúk\030Find Khêjiba in the girls' bedroom\tYou need to secure the safety of Kotráka Saiya's family by getting them out of the palace. You should find Kotráka Saiya's three daughters and son, Otibúk and speak to loyal guards nearby.\n4\tFind Khêjiba\tYou need to secure the safety of Kotráka Saiya's family by getting them out of the palace. You should find Khêjiba somewhere in the palace royal quarters.\n5\tTalk to Dark Priestess Barkhuráni\tKotráka Saiya's sister, Barkhuráni, will not allow her to leave with the children. You should defeat Dark Priestess Barkhuráni.\n6\tDefeat Dark Priestess Barkhuráni\tKotráka Saiya's sister, Barkhuráni, will not allow her to leave with the children. You should defeat Dark Priestess Barkhuráni.\n7\tTalk to Kotráka Saiya\tYou have secured the safety of the royal family. You should talk to Kotráka Saiya.\n8\tReturn to the entrance of the royal quarters\tYou have secured the safety of the royal family. You should return to the entrance of the royal quarters and speak to the servant standing by.\n9\tTalk to Kotráka Saiya\tKotráka Saiya will now hold up her end of the deal and show you the secret way into the city. You should speak to Kotráka Saiya and meet up with your allies.\n10\tTalk to Mizâdi\tMizâdi has set up camp at the secret entrance to the city. You should talk to Mizâdi at Nashûbu.\n",
[9551]="7006C702\n1\tVisit Ashâmi and Raphûz at their home in Urmâkh\tAshâmi told you she and Raphûz intend to fight alongside one another against whatever the great evil stirring in Shagâna proves to be. She hopes you will visit them at their home in Urmâkh.\n2\tCollect your letter at Ashâmi and Raphûz's home in Urmâkh\tYour friends and their things are gone from the home. There is a note bearing your name left behind. You should collect and read the note you found.\n3\tRead the letter left for you by your friends Ashâmi and Raphûz\tYou found a letter at the home once occupied by Raphûz and Ashâmi in the settlement of Urmâkh. You wonder what the letter might say.\n4\tTalk to Raphûz in Urash Dâr\tThough the letter did not say directly Ashâmi and Raphûz went on to Urash Dâr, all you know of the pair and your journeys lead to their taking the fight to the heart of the enemy. Should you find yourself in Urash Dâr, you should look there for your friends.\n",
[9552]="70009E74\n1\tTalk to Mayor Wat Mudbottom\tMayor Wat Mudbottom is at Hoarhallow far to the west of Glán Vraig, through the Grimwood Forest, on the banks of the Hoarwell River. Beset by the Enemy, the Hobbits of Hoarhallow are a hardy and proud people. Their Mayor, Wat Mudbottom, leads them and refuses to give up the land they own to the forces of Angmar. Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn directed you to speak with Wat Mudbottom.\n",
[9553]="70000049\n1\tDeliver the Statue of The Maiden to Hunulf Munce\030Collect the Statue of a Maiden\tThe goblins of Minas Eriol are in possession of the statue. Hunulf directed you to seek out the greatest discovery made by the Eglain, a statue dredged from the swamps of the Lone-lands.\n",
[9554]="70048C9A\n1\tDefeat enemies in Kala-gijak (total: 30)\tUruks and trolls can be found in Kala-gijak. You should defeat enemies in Kala-gijak.\n2\tCompleted.\t\n",
[9555]="7001C070\n1\tTalk to Kekkonen at the Tornstones\030Collect etched stones (total: 3)\tStones bearing the historical markings of the Earth-kin may be found on the trolls in the woods bordering Harloeg. Kekkonen at the Tornstones desires to collect and maintain the history of his people. He dispatched you to fight the trolls of Harloeg to collect the stolen stones bearing the Earth-kin's history.\n",
[9556]="7006C6F2\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz at his home in Urmâkh\tAshâmi is genuinely pleased to see you and told you to go and speak with Raphûz. She expects that he will be even more pleased. You can find him at their home in Urmâkh.\n2\tSpeak with Raphûz at Numûru's post in Urmâkh\030Speak with Ashâmi at Numûru's post in Urmâkh\tRaphûz and Ashâmi asked you to attend their meeting with Numûru, the right hand of Mizâdi Shâra-ingari. You should meet them at Numûru's post in Urmâkh.\n3\tSpeak with Numûru at his post in Urmâkh\tAshâmi and Raphûz both asked if you would speak with Numûru about their character. The soldier professed concern about their resolve. You can find Numûru at his post in Urmâkh.\n4\tDeliver the map to Ashâmi at Numûru's post in Urmâkh\030Deliver the map to Raphûz at Nûmuru's post in Urmâkh\tNumûru supplied you with two maps and asked you to give them to Ashâmi and Raphûz. Deliver the maps to Ashâmi and Raphûz at Numûru's post in Urmâkh.\n5\tSpeak with Ashâmi at her home in Urmâkh\tAshâmi and Raphûz were provided orders from Numûru to prove their courage against their fears. They both reacted differently and asked you to meet them back at their home in Urmâkh.\n",
[9557]="7006C6FF\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz at his home in Urmâkh\tAshâmi is ready to return to Numûru at his post in Urmâkh. She wants you to ensure that Raphûz is also ready to return to Mizâdi's captain. You will find Raphûz at their home in Urmâkh.\n2\tSpeak with Numûru about Ashâmi and Raphûz at his post in Urmâkh\tRaphûz and Ashâmi are both ready to return to Numûru. They ask you to meet them at Numûru's post in Urmâkh to see the result of their efforts.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz at Numûru's post in Urmâkh\030Speak with Ashâmi at Numûru's post in Urmâkh\tNumûru said there is one more task that Ashâmi and Raphûz must complete together. The two were surprised they had not done enough. He instructed you to speak to them at his post in Urmâkh.\n4\tSpeak with Ashâmi at her home in Urmâkh\tAshâmi and Raphûz returned to their home in Urmâkh to discuss how they will undertake the next challenge. They wish to speak to you at their home in Urmâkh before they go.\n",
[9558]="7006C573\n1\tDeliver the letters to Sigénik\030Read the letter home if you wish\tNangar returned the untranslated and translated letters to you with instruction to deliver them to Sigénik. He believes Sigénik is better fit to direct you than he.\n2\tDeliver the letters to the Amalíbi\030Read the letter if you wish\tSigénik directed you to climb the crags to the east to find an oasis where the rebels, and their leader Amalíbi. You are to deliver the letters to her.\n",
[9559]="7002CB2E\n1\tDefeat Oathbreakers in Ost Celebrant (total: 12)\tTreacherous Oathbreakers can be found throughout Ost Celebrant.\n2\tTalk to Doron\tDoron is within Ost Celebrant. If he has left your side, call him with your horn.\n",
[9560]="7003FC03\n1\tFollow the river Blackroot south to Morlad\tMorlad can be found to the south and slightly west of the Paths of the Dead in Blackroot Vale. Ludhír has asked you to travel to Morlad, the chief settlement in the Blackroot Vale, and speak with the steward.\n2\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tMalthellam can be found in Morlad, to the south-west of the Paths of the Dead. Ludhír has asked that you meet with Malthellam, the steward of the Vale. Gondor's armies have ridden east and many troubles face the people that remain.\n",
[9561]="70016B8B\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Drû-garmadh (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found at Drû-garmadh, south-east of Mekhem-bizru. Alrekur is concerned about the number of Orcs setting up camps in the Dimrill Dale and wants you to thin their number.\n2\tTalk to Alrekur at Mekhem-bizru\tAlrekur is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh. Alrekur will want to know the Orcs at Drû-garmadh have been thinned.\n",
[9562]="7002F01A\n1\tDefeat Orcs or Uruks on Amon Hen (total: 8)\tOrcs and Uruks can be found all over Amon Hen. Maedal has asked you to defeat as many of the Orcs on Amon Hen as you can, in order to make the rescue of her friend Drafli Broadshield easier.\n2\tTalk to Maedal\tMaedal is on Amon Hen, hidden in plain sight. You have defeated Orcs and Uruks on Amon Hen and should return now to Maedal to tell her of your successes.\n",
[9563]="700442FB\n1\tDestroy Sûhalar tents at Parth Duin (total: 6)\030Destroy Sûhalar barricades (total: 8)\tParth Duin is located east of Crithost. You should destroy Easterling tents and destroy their barricades before the farm becomes a full fledged encampment.\n2\tTalk to Tolwin\tTolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost. You should speak with Tolwin.\n",
[9564]="70042F83\n1\tDagor's men can be found scattered east and south of Arnach. You should find Dagor's men and send them back to Arnach, post-haste.\t\n2\tTalk to Dagor\tDagor can be found within the walls of Arnach's keep. You have found all of Dagor's men and sent them back to Arnach. You should return to him to tell him this has been done.\n",
[9565]="7006BCD0\n1\tReach Ishegir's first favourite spot\tAngârmu has asked you to check for his camel, Ishegir, at his first favourte spot to the west, past the big rock.\n2\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at his first favourite spot\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at his first favourite spot near big rock to the west of which Angârmu spoke.\n3\tReach Ishegir's second favourite spot\tThere was no sign of Ishegir at his first favourite spot. He may be at his second favourite spot near the river's edge to the east.\n4\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location.\n5\tReach Ishegir's third favourite spot\tThere was no sign of Ishegir at his second favourite spot. Perhaps you will find him at his third favourite spot that Angârmu told you of, near the Pools of Kudím to the north of here.\n6\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location\tUse the look emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location.\n7\tReturn to Angârmu with news of Ishegir\tReturn to Angârmu with news of Ishegir after having checked all of his favourite spots he had suggested.\n",
[9566]="70041C7B\n1\tBurn banners in Hata Kebir (total: 10)\030Defeat Half-trolls in Hata Kebir (total: 4)\030Defeat Corsair captains in Hata Kebir (quantity: see journal)\tHata Kebir can be found far to the south-east of Ost Anglebed in Lebennin. Nimithil has asked you to assault the Haradrim and Corsair forces in Hata Kebir.\n2\tTalk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed\tNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin. You have slain many of the forces in Hata Kebir and set flame to their banners. You should now return to Nimithil.\n",
[9567]="70035740\n1\tDismantle White Hand tents in Drû Vádokan (total: 3)\tTents of the White Hand can be found throughout Drû Vádokan in north-west Balewood. You should dismantle any Orc-tents you find while assaulting the White Hand encampment.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have successfully dismantled many tents of the White Hand in the Balewood. Without their shelter, the Orcs will find maintaining their presence in the Balewood far more challenging.\n",
[9568]="70015226\n1\tUse the mixture on Kraibag\tKraibag is somewhere in the Water-works, near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar. Ansurr told you to find Kraibag, the most powerful of the infested Orcs, and use the mixture the dwarves gave you on him to determine its effect.\n2\tDefeat Kraibag\tKraibag is somewhere in the Water-works near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar. The mixture appeared to have no effect on Kraibag. He must still be defeated to ensure the safety of the dwarves of the Water-works.\n3\tTalk to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh\tAnsurr is at Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters. Return to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh and inform him that even though the concoction they gave you did not work, in fact quite the opposite, you still defeated Kraibag.\n",
})
